From 2909b7afff7e2e2d1d918c0cb6fcb1fe4c859b07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolai Protasov <nprotaso@amd.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:51:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] [AMD] Use the FlyDSL hc_mix kernel for Qwen3.8
 hyper-connections on gfx950

GatedResidual's mix projection dispatches to aiter.ops.flydsl.hc_mix (with
prepacked, cached weights) for 1-16 BF16 rows on gfx950 when AITER ships the
kernel; SGLANG_AITER_HC_MIX=0 turns it off. SGLANG_HC_COMBINE_SPLIT gates the
split gate+apply hc_combine and defaults off on ROCm, where both halves sit
at the launch floor and one fused kernel is faster.

From amd-nprotaso/sglang qwen_3_8_improvement: 0feb9bf330, 7c0933bae1,
c58e9fad01 and 19dff56c7f. Needs the AITER hc_mix kernel.
